cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this app, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references.
type: software
title: stim-dose-response
abstract: 'Physiological responses to nerve stimulation and their dose-response, for any species and protocol: baseline,
  during and after each stimulation train for every heart-rate, blood-pressure and respiration series (or any series.csv
  of the same shape); change, peak change, time to peak and recovery; dose-response per subject and pooled (subject
  as a random effect, statsmodels MixedLM) with Hill, Boltzmann, linear or no dependence chosen by AIC (Akaike 1974),
  thresholds, EC50 and bootstrap confidence intervals (Efron 1979); amplitude x frequency response surfaces; and
  the amplitude where the heart-rate response changes sign, after the neural fulcrum of Ardell et al. (2017).'
authors:
- name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
contact:
- given-names: Joost
  family-names: Wagenaar
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5925-5451
  affiliation: University of Pennsylvania
repository-code: https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/stim-dose-response
license: Apache-2.0
